# Frontend CI & hygiene

This repo is `VictoryBowlingSoftware/react-frontend`. Backend is a separate git root (`fastapi-backend` / workspace `backend/`).

## Before claiming done (match CI)

```bash
npm run check:vibe-ship
npm run check:god-components
npm run check:datetime
npm run lint:api
npm run test:cov
npm run build
npm run test:e2e -- --grep-invert @fullflow
```

Merge-blocking CI job id: `vibe-ship-invariants` (`docs/MERGE_GATES.md`).

Also run `npm test` / `npm run lint` locally when touching broad UI. Director e2e must use **`seedDirectorSession` + `page.route` mocks**, not live `loginAsDirector` against a missing backend. Reserve `@fullflow` for real-backend suites. Prefer `npm run check:god-components` when touching large pages/workspaces **or any file listed in** `scripts/check-god-component-sizes.mjs`. If over ceiling, extract in the same PR (`file-size-limits.mdc`, `large-print-payloads.mdc`).

## UI / test coupling

If you change headings, tab copy, CTAs, or remove/rename components - **update matching unit and e2e tests in the same change**. Specs that still assert `"Coming Soon"` after shipping real UI (or after hiding a deferred tab) are defective tests. Do not reintroduce unfinished surfaces — see `no-unfinished-surfaces.mdc`.

## Never commit

- `.env`, credentials, local-only artifacts
- Push only when asked. For commit shape / "commit and push" splitting, follow `commit-cadence.mdc` (small sequential commits, not one fat dump).
## Language standards

TypeScript / React conventions live in `typescript-best-practices.mdc` and `typescript-hygiene.mdc` — follow those on new and touched `.ts`/`.tsx` files.
